 of unmanned intelligence. The company has a Partnership with Havoc to develop open-architecture autonomous maritime defense systems. Red Cat Holdings, Inc. is based in South Salt Lake, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey M. Thompson | Founder, President, CEO & Chairman | Age 61 | Compensation: $273,406 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 244 people. Revenue per employee of $167K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 85%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $43K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Red Cat Holdings, Inc. is a micro-cap industrials business with a $288M market cap on $41M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +85% over the past three years and +92% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -46% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $96M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Stock-based comp at 26% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (29.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 173% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +6.2% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 104% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Red Cat (RCAT) Stock Could Be Pricey After Weak Sales News","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-rcat/red-cat-holdings/news/red-cat-rcat-stock-could-be-pricey-after-weak-sales-news","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795756547.756,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Red Cat Just Dropped 27% in a Week. Will RCAT Stock Hit $1.5